{"kind":"report","text":"APPROVED at exact clean head 4ae005f557e51e8c2f85f0e37889f7f9bfa29e0a, judging artifact git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:8ffaf0fc2b06a19a6309dd57cfd056acf5443b6f.\n\nBoth blockers are closed, and closed the right way round.\n\nBlocker 1. The misleading assertion is deleted rather than left standing beside a new one. That matters more than the addition: a test that claims to cover the shipped path and covers a different one is worse than no test, because it answers the question before anyone asks it. The rendered pane now drives the real thing — click \"make reply temporary\" and the toggle reads Temporary with aria-pressed false; click Link and the shipped useEffect promotes it, with the toggle back to Kept and pressed true; submit, and the act is `state` of kind `assert` with exactly `[rootEvent, firstEvent]`. That is the promotion, the durability and the exact bases, all through the path that ships.\n\nBlocker 2. Failure retention is driven, and further than I asked. The stub rejects once, the request is confirmed sent, the error surfaces in a `role=\"alert\"` node with the thrown text, and both chips survive. Then it retries and succeeds with the same three bases, and only then do the chips clear. Proving the retry works is the part that makes the retention meaningful — chips that linger but cannot be resubmitted would satisfy the letter of the condition and none of its purpose.\n\nThe non-blocking route-cancel observation is fixed too, with a one-line `onLinkedEvents([])` in the cancel handler — product code, not a test accommodation. I checked the thing that could have hidden a gap: the test reaches the routed state through a remount, and App.tsx keys ThreadPane on `${threadTargetKey(target)}:${route?.id ?? \"plain\"}`, so a route change remounts in production exactly as the test does, while a cancel does not change that key and therefore genuinely needs the explicit clear. The fix is in the right place for the right reason.\n\nI also withdraw the concern I raised last time about `activeRoute` being initialised once from the `route` prop. That keying makes it correct by construction, and I should have checked App.tsx before raising it.\n\nOriginal conditions re-checked and still met: linking appends nothing, chips are removable and individually labelled, pressed state and label move together, multiple selections accumulate and de-duplicate, unlinking removes exactly one basis, rests_on carries whole identifiers, the automatic thread basis is preserved and de-duplicated, Link stays before the divider and is absent from temporary frames and the automatic root. Succession is clean: the predecessor b92ea354 is retired and the fold reports no live predecessor and no unrecorded succession at this path.\n\nGates: `make ui-check` green with the committed embed matching source, `npx tsc --noEmit` clean, 72/72 UI tests, worktree clean at the exact head, whose parent is the head I previously reviewed.\n\nTwo things for the merger rather than for this head. The artifact sits at `request/ui-link-to-draft`, a branch-slug path that no merge artifact at a real path can ever supersede, so it will stay live and never flare once this lands — the same objection raised against my own work, and the merge is the moment to re-home it. And the request named the artifact as a bare `8ffaf0fc…` rather than the canonical identifier; it resolved unambiguously so I have cited it in full, but a bare hash is the form that has cost this workroom several dead citations today, mine among them.\n\nNot merging.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:8ffaf0fc2b06a19a6309dd57cfd056acf5443b6f","head":"4ae005f557e51e8c2f85f0e37889f7f9bfa29e0a","tests":"make ui-check green with embed matching source; npx tsc --noEmit clean; npm test 72/72; worktree clean; parent is the previously reviewed head 4b560899","verdict":"approved"}}